WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.267
-Nice to see you, buddy.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.767
Good to see you.
You told me before the show,

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.434
you're very,
very skinny right now

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.701
because you're preparing
for another role.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.167
-Yeah, yeah,
I'm a little bit light,

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.968
so I was concerned
about wearing,

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.300
you know,
such baggy clothes, but.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.367
Yeah. Yeah, I've lost
a decent amount of weight

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.567
to play a prisoner of war.
So I'm a little bit concerned

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:19.801
because I think I look like --

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:21.701
I've seen a few photos
on the Internet of me...

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.167
-No, you look good.
-...as Slender Man.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.033
-You know what's so funny?

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:29.167
Everyone keeps -- I've been
reading articles about you,

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.868
and everyone keeps going
how tall are you?

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.801
-I know.
-They're concerned about your --

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.300
You're tall.
How tall are you?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.100
-I'm 6'5", 197 centimeters.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.067
-Thank you.
-6'5".

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.367
And was that always the thing
when you were growing up

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.634
and everyone saying,
"oh, he's so tall"?

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.367
-Yeah, I was born 6'5".
-Yeah.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:49.133
Wow. Amazing. Wow.
Yeah. Still delivering.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:52.100
Yeah. He's still coming. Yeah.
We know it's a boy,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.534
but we just don't know
how tall it is.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:54.734
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:56.667
-No, no, I mean,
I've been this big

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.200
since I was 15 or 16.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.701
And I'm pretty sure I've been
making movies for 5 or 6 years.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.667
So it's come as a surprise
to me now that -- Yeah.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.868
-That's wild. Yeah.
Congratulations, by the way.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.133
You're playing -- You're Elvis.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.534
-Yeah, man.
-That's so fun.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.467
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.033
-Last time you were on our show,

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:18.834
you surprised your parents too,
and took them to a Knick game.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.567
-Yeah, we went to the Knicks.
-Which is kind of fun

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.767
because Julius Randle is here
tonight.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.834
But here you are.
How was the Knick game?

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.167
-[ Laughs ] My mom.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.167
-There you are there.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.968
-Aw. Taking photos.
She's taking pics.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.868
-It was great, man.
It was awesome.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.734
It's always a blast. Yeah.
-Was she taking -- This

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:35.868
is her taking a picture of you
on the jumbotron?

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.300
-Yeah, of the big screen. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.701
-That's a proud mom right there.

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:41.834
-Yeah.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.334
-That is a great job, mom,
I love you.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.367
That was awesome.
Like, "That's my boy!"

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:47.734
-That's my mom.
-"That's my son up there."

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.734
-Yeah.
Meanwhile, I'm sat right there.

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.133
-Exactly.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.467
She's also on the jumbotron.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.434
Yeah, but it's not about her.
It's not about mom.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.667
It's about you.
-Get out of here.

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.534
-Yeah. Did you meet any --

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.167
Did you meet any celebs while
you were there?

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:02.434
-I kind of -- I saw
Spike Lee from afar.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.801
And I like to think
that he went like this.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:07.501
-Yeah, he did, he did.
I think he did.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.934
-You know?
-Yeah.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.467
-Let's talk about "Priscilla."

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.501
You get to play Elvis Presley.
-Yeah.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:15.200
-Is there pressure on you there
when you're playing it?

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.701
-I mean, it wasn't --

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:19.934
it wasn't on my list
of people to play.

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.033
It was definitely -- It was
a little bit terrifying. Yeah.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.300
-But growing up, were you
an Elvis fan or did you...?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.434
-No. The most I knew of Elvis
was in "Lilo and Stitch,"

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:28.400
that kind of...
-Wow.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.367
-Yeah, that was my -- Yeah.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.601
-Isn't that amazing?
-Yeah.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.033
Which is a lot.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.868
-Yeah.
When you were auditioning,

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.300
did you go, "I got this,"
or you go,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.501
like, did you nail the voice or
what did you...?

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.534
-I had -- Sofia had sent me

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:43.033
these sides that said Elvis,
and I kind of just was like,

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.601
"There's just no chance
that this is happening."

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.767
So I watched this clip of him

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.400
when he came back from the Army
in Germany.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.033
And I read the lines
for like 15 minutes

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.934
and then shot two takes
and, you know,

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.701
not thinking that
it would go anywhere.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.167
I'm pretty sure my voice
for that was like...

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Deep vocalizing ]

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I would have done that.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.534
-I think it was just...
-"Hey, what's going on?"

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:08.300
"Jimmy, we're good. Don't even
put yourself on tape."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.868
-But she liked it, you know.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.467
-I mean, it's Sofia Coppola.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.067
-Yeah.
-I mean, was that also

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.934
intimidating too, working
with -- having her direct you?

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.634
-I think it was just exciting.

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.300
Like, that was just, like,
pure bliss.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.534
That was the only reason.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.300
You know, the whole time
I was trying to

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.634
take it like I was making
"Blue Valentine" or something.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.067
Just like a straight-up
relationship drama

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:29.467
without Elvis and Priscilla
for Sofia Coppola.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.200
That was like the goal.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.067
-We don't --
It focuses on the relationship

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.400
between you and Priscilla,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.267
but you do get to wear
a couple of awesome jumpsuits.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.601
-Yeah.
-And that's got to feel cool,

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.801
right?
-Yeah, 100%.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.834
I mean, it was -- as soon
as you put that --

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.367
because you kind of --
you pull them on

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:47.968
and you zip them
from right here,

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:50.467
which is where all his,
you know, his energy was.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.667
-The chi.
-Yeah. The chi was just

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.367
deeply centered and --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.601
I understand.
-You zip it up.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.267
It comes up
to right about here.

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.334
-It doesn't go further.
-Bow!

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.501
-Bang. Yeah. Wow. Okay. Yeah.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:01.934
Yeah. Okay. Here we go.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.767
Please stop doing that.
Yeah.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.434
People have 3-D television sets
at home,

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:08.467
and they're getting concerned.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. -

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.400
The movie's
getting great reviews.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.701
Congratulations on that.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:14.267
I saw that it got
an eight-minute standing ovation

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.701
at the Venice Film Festival.
Congratulations.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:17.801
-Thank you.

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:22.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.901
-Here's my question.
My question is what do you

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.634
do for eight minutes
when people are clapping?

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.100
Trust me, I'll never find out.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.167
When people clap for you --

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:35.501
I mean, the movie ends
and then eight minutes start?

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.067
-Yeah, basically,
the credits roll

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:40.067
and you're kind of waiting on
bated breath, with bated breath.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.267
You know, are they going
to enjoy the film or not?

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:45.434
And then they start clapping.
And for the first 10,

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.300
15 seconds,
you know, it's wonderful.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.067
It's nice to have the praise.
-Of course.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:52.434
-And then it keeps going
and it keeps going.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:53.701
-But do you look to Sofia and --

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:56.601
-You look at Sofia,
and she's a professional

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.400
and everyone -- and Priscilla is
standing there

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.133
looking beautiful, you know,
taking in what's deserved.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.501
And then I kind of look
to like the press team

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.934
and they're like, "Go, go."

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:08.667
So you have to walk down
these steps to, like,

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.367
get them going even more,

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.067
but without, like --
-Without doing that.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:14.801
-Without going like, "Get up."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.267
You have to go and just
kind of be humble.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:17.701
-Yeah. You're like,
"Well, I guess..."

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.167
-"I don't know. If you want to.
Yeah. I mean, we're here."

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.434
-Yeah. But I mean seven,

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.434
seven minutes is a long time,
you know?

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.601
-Gosh. Congratulations.
That's a cool moment.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:26.934
You don't forget.
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.400
-By the way, it was great
to meet your sister backstage.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.267
-Yeah. She's here somewhere.
-I love that she's here.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.934
That's awesome. Shout-out.
That's cool.

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:35.000
I love that you stay close
to your family. I love that.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.701
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.334
Here's Jacob Elordi
in "Priscilla."

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:39.601
Take a look at this.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:43.567
♪♪

00:05:43.567 --> 00:05:45.400
-Prints take away
from your look.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.434
-Oh, it's like a forest.

00:05:47.434 --> 00:05:49.534
-I like this one.
-Solid suits you better.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:52.100
And I hate brown.
Reminds me of the army.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:59.868
♪♪

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:02.133
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:10.133
♪♪

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.501
Mm.

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:14.200
Black hair and more eye makeup.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.534
Make your eyes stand out more.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:17.701
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:18.868
-4:00, boys. We got to go.

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.400
Barbecue's waiting. Let's go.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.834
-Yeah, bud, you had it
even down.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.834
You had everything
down to a tee.

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:27.200
-Thank you, man.
-Jacob Elordi, everybody.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.167
"Priscilla" is in theaters
November 3rd.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.567
More with Jacob
when we come back.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:32.634
Stick around, everybody.

